+cost grid {zero, realistic, conservative} using the repository's canonical
+realistic model (commission_per_trade=2.0, commission_per_share=0.003,
+slippage_cents=2.0, slippage_proportional=0.0005; conservative = 2x); same
+walk-forward regime gate as the prior momentum checks (train=252/test=84/warmup=60/
+overlap=60, 4 contiguous volatility blocks, min 400 bars/segment); matched
+coin-flip null run under the SAME cost config on the same segments.
+
+DECISIVE FINDING — the momentum signal is not momentum. `research.backtest.momentum_signals`
+computes `np.mean(np.log(closes[i-lookback+1:i+1]))`: the mean log PRICE LEVEL,
+not the mean log RETURN. With every adjusted close above 1.0 this is positive for
+every lookback, so the emitted weight is constant +1 (always long) on 9/10 tickers
+(NVDA mostly long). Verified directly (`existing == always_long` for 9/10). The
+admitted "momentum edge" is therefore an always-long large-cap drift/beta position.
+The prior artifacts still reproduce exactly under this signal (cross-consistency
+vs `momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json` = True for all 10 tickers), so the conflict
+is the signal definition, not the data or the walk-forward machinery.
+
+Cost-sensitivity result:
+- Existing (admitted) signal: medians are essentially flat across costs (universe
+  mean 0.0612 / 0.0603 / 0.0595 at lookback 5), because constant-dollar sizing keeps
+  per-bar turnover tiny relative to the drift. Its "cost robustness" pertains to a
+  drift/beta position, not momentum. The single COST_FRAGILE label (MSFT, lookback 5)
+  is a null-dispersion verdict flip (candidate median flat +0.062; null dispersion
+  collapses 0.0081 -> 0.0019), not cost erosion.
+- Corrected past-only momentum signal (long when closes[i] > closes[i-lookback],
+  evaluated locally in the check; the framework function was NOT changed here):
+  10/10 NO_EDGE at every lookback 3/5/10 even at ZERO cost. There is no momentum
+  edge to "survive" costs; costs only push the few small zero-cost positives negative
+  (AMZN 0.0006 -> -0.013, GOOGL 0.0024 -> -0.0024, AAPL 0.034 -> 0.028).
+
